<title>INDIA: India says to take up farm subsidies at WTO.</title>
<headline>India says to take up farm subsidies at WTO.</headline>
<dateline>CALCUTTA 1997-01-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Minister Bolla Buli Ramaiah said on Saturday that India planned to raise the issue of agricultural subsidies at the next ministerial meeting of the World Trade Organisation (WTO).</p>
<p>In response to a question at an international business conference, Ramaiah said high agricultural subsidies in some countries were hindering agricultural exports from developing countries.</p>
<p>&quot;Subsidies offered by various countries are much more than what we are doing in this country,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;At the next ministerial conference, we will certainly take up this issue,&quot; Ramaiah said. &quot;We have to make more and more agricultural exports,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Some developing nations have criticised subsidies in various Western countries and Japan.</p>
</text>
